# Every path in this repository is owned by its maintainer.
#
# REPO-BASELINE.md §1: the failure this prevents is a security-relevant path
# merged without the right reviewer. In a single-maintainer repository that is a
# low bar — but the file is also the machine-readable answer to "who reviews
# this", which is what makes it worth committing before there is a second
# contributor rather than after the first surprise merge.

*                           @konradcinkusz

# The paths called out below are ROADMAP.md §5's protected paths, and the two
# lists are meant to stay identical. A change to any of them breaks EVERY later
# pull request rather than only its own:
#
#   main.tex          the document root — broken, nothing builds
#   mybeamer.cls      loads every package, defines every section colour, and
#                     owns \RepoURL and the footline
#   mybeamer.sty      defines \QuestionSlide, \AnswerTitle and \Difficulty, on
#                     which all 269 cards now depend
#   .github/workflows the build itself
#   scripts/          the card linter and the secret scanner's local half; a
#                     broken validator turns every later PR into
#                     three-retries-and-force-merge
#   .gitleaks.toml    a scanner that passes vacuously is worse than none
#
# areas/*.tex are deliberately NOT here. A LaTeX error in one card does break the
# build, but it is contained, obvious, and named by the compiler.

/main.tex                   @konradcinkusz
/mybeamer.cls               @konradcinkusz
/mybeamer.sty               @konradcinkusz
/.github/workflows/         @konradcinkusz
/scripts/                   @konradcinkusz
/.gitleaks.toml             @konradcinkusz
